<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT-Campbell Soup raised.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT-Campbell Soup raised.</headline>
<text>
<p>- Deutsche Morgan Grenfell raised Campbell Soup to buy from hold, citing announced restructuring plans.</p>
<p>- Earnings estimates were raised to $3.60 a share for the fiscal year to July 1997 from $3.50. Earnings for fiscal 1998 were estimated at $4.15.</p>
<p>- A $1.5 billion &quot;Dutch auction&quot; share repurchase program was forecast to potentially boost earnings by $0.05 a share.</p>
<p>- Benefits from a $200 million cost-savings program were forecast at around $0.50-$0.60 a share by fiscal 1998.</p>
</text>
